  "disclosure": "Measured on the 27 Oct 2026 draw and shown unranked until that draw is equated to the reference scale. The composed checkpoint ibm-granite/granite-switch-4.1-8b@fb4aa7877e13e5fe09ca328713dc1db72a3f93ce identifies its decision adapter as revision 4.1.1. It ran with generative-computing/granite-switch@43ccd291a176507ae4ed5af293f8f2d947c0d451; no base-plus-adapter recomposition or direct PEFT substitute was used. The 27 October revision updated the decision adapter weights; archived Git/LFS metadata identifies the pinned 28 October HEAD change as README-only. This metadata is not tensor-level proof that every base tensor is unchanged. The source and tokenizer files were hash-verified before use. Upstream wheels were hash-locked, and Debian libgomp1 12.2.0-14+deb12u1 and libnuma1 2.0.16-1 were recorded. The plugin source was registered read-only without running author build scripts; composer and tutorial subtrees were excluded. Source checks and isolation are not an exhaustive audit of all upstream code or custom kernels. Training data and overlap with public or sealed evaluation data were not independently inspected; no contamination audit is claimed. The text-only composed decision recipe differs from the model card's public Decision Index system-prompt recipe, so its reported evaluation numbers are not transferred here. The semantic context limit is 131,072 tokens including the generated token; backend allocation had room for the measured draw and public envelope without lowering the semantic limit. Whole states and ordered options were preserved: no truncations or native refusals, 1,500/1,500 HTTP 200 responses, 818,484 input and 1,500 output tokens, zero usage mismatches and zero native-behavior deviations. No prompt permutation averaging, response repair or scored retry was used. REPLAY VARIABILITY: 7 of 50 repeat requests were bit-identical, with zero argmax flips and maximum absolute probability difference 0.0312263773757529. Exact probability reproducibility is not established and its cause was not independently diagnosed. Repeats were recorded only; no scored response was averaged, repaired or replaced. The public same-engine label re-extraction check was fixed before this measurement at a 5e-2 absolute ceiling, with exact label sets, own-winner consistency and an explicit near-tie allowance. This passed; it is not a cross-backend equivalence test or a post-score adjustment. Scored latency: p50 0.028615256 seconds, p95 0.054891614, p99 0.113791849 and maximum 10.999436637. Five decisions exceeded ten seconds; under the ten-second rule they count as wrong answers. Earlier setup, public parity and timing attempts stopped before any sealed input. This is the first completed use on this draw, with the declared backend selection, public repeat ceiling and typed-overhead corrections fixed beforehand. The measured base remains ibm-granite/granite-4.1-8b; its price uses the explicitly labelled granite-4.2-8b sibling estimate. Granite is outside the six calibrated Gemma/Qwen throughput classes, so the existing cost method keeps that estimate and supplies no GPU-time component.",
